(a) Material strength properties must be based on enough tests of material meeting specifications to establish design values on a statistical basis. (b) The design values must be chosen so that the probability of any structure being understrength because of material variations is extremely remote. (c) Unless they are inapplicable in a particular case, the design values must be those contained in the following publications (obtainable from the Superintendent of Documents, Government Printing Office, Washington, D.C., 20402):
MIL-HDBK-5, &quot;Metallic Materials and Elements for Flight Vehicle Structure&quot;;
MIL-HDBK-17, &quot;Plastics for Flight Vehicles&quot;;
ANC-18, &quot;Design of Wood Aircraft Structures&quot;; and
MIL-HDBK-23, &quot;Composite Construction for Flight Vehicles&quot;.

